/S /H4
/P 179 0 R
/T (PROBLEM: Healthcare today is reactive, fragmented, and overloaded. Patients often delay consulting doctors due to cost or uncertainty, while doctors spend valuable time on basic triage. Many patients struggle to understand reports, manage medications, and follow care plans. The absence of continuous, intelligent health monitoring leads to delayed diagnosis, poor adherence, and increased healthcare burden.)
/E (PROBLEM: Healthcare today is reactive, fragmented, and overloaded. Patients often delay consulting doctors due to cost or uncertainty, while doctors spend valuable time on basic triage. Many patients struggle to understand reports, manage medications, and follow care plans. The absence of continuous, intelligent health monitoring leads to delayed diagnosis, poor adherence, and increased healthcare burden.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
